{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.CechColimitConverse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.CechColimitConverse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.CechColimit","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Shapes.Pullback.HasPullback","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Grothendieck"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.PresheafCentralExtension.cechObstruction_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.PresheafCentralExtension.cechObstruction_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L276-L304","doc":"**Cover-independent lifting criterion.** On a directed system of covers\n(for example, the covers of a site with pullbacks, `isCoverDirected_topology`),\nthe colimit obstruction class of `γ` is trivial iff `γ` lifts to an\n`𝓔`-torsor on some admissible refinement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.cechClass_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.cechClass_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L234-L256","doc":"**The converse, for cocycles.** On a directed system of covers, a cocycle's\nclass in the colimit `Ȟ²` is trivial iff it becomes a coboundary on some\nadmissible refinement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.eventuallyTrivial_step_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.eventuallyTrivial_step_iff","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L205-L231","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.CoverCocycle.EventuallyTrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.CoverCocycle.EventuallyTrivial","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L196-L200","doc":"A cover-cocycle pair **becomes trivial** if its pullback to some admissible\nrefinement is a coboundary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.isCoverDirected_topology","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.isCoverDirected_topology","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L184-L188","doc":"**The covers of a site are directed.** For a Grothendieck topology on a\ncategory with pullbacks, \"generates a covering sieve\" is a directed predicate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.isCoverDirected_of_meet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.isCoverDirected_of_meet","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L179-L182","doc":"Admissibility closed under meets gives a directed system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.IsCoverDirected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.IsCoverDirected","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L173-L177","doc":"A predicate on covers is **directed** if any two admissible covers have an\nadmissible common refinement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.generate_meet_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.generate_meet_mem","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L167-L171","doc":"For a Grothendieck topology, the meet of two covering covers is covering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.sieve_inf_le_meet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.sieve_inf_le_meet","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L159-L165","doc":"The meet's sieve contains the intersection of the two sieves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.sieve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.sieve","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L155-L157","doc":"The sieve generated by a cover. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.meetRight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.meetRight","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L148-L153","doc":"The meet refines the second cover. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.meetLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.meetLeft","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L141-L146","doc":"The meet refines the first cover. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.meet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.meet","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L134-L139","doc":"The common refinement of two covers of `X`: the family of pullbacks\n`V_j ×_X W_k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.pull_pull_ev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.pull_pull_ev","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L127-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.Refines.comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.Refines.comp","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L120-L125","doc":"Refinements compose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.Refines.id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.Cover.Refines.id","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L114-L118","doc":"The identity refinement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.Rel.of_ev_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.TwoCocycle.Rel.of_ev_eq","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L103-L108","doc":"`Rel` only sees the values of the second cocycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.pullTwoCocycle_rel_of_two_refinements","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.pullTwoCocycle_rel_of_two_refinements","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L80-L93","doc":"**Prism homotopy.** Two refinement maps pull a 2-cocycle of a commutative\npresheaf back to cohomologous 2-cocycles. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.prismCochain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.prismCochain","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L71-L78","doc":"The prism 1-cochain comparing two refinements `(r, f)` and `(r', f')`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.core_prism","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CentralExtension.CechGerbe.core_prism","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/CechColimitConverse.lean#L56-L65","doc":"The algebraic core of the prism homotopy, in a commutative group. ","signatureChunk":0}]}